, Arslanbaeva L, Sidorova T, Lopez MG, et al. Mitochondrial deacetylase Sirt3 reduces vascular dysfunction and hypertension while Sirt3 depletion in essential hypertension is linked to vascular inflammation and oxidative stress. Circ Res. 2020;126:439&#x2013;52.</Citation><ArticleIdList><ArticleId IdType="doi">10.1161/CIRCRESAHA.119.315767</ArticleId><ArticleId IdType="pmc">PMC7035170</ArticleId><ArticleId IdType="pubmed">31852393</ArticleId></ArticleIdList></Reference><Reference><Citation>M&#xfc;ller AL, Dhalla NS. Differences in concentric cardiac hypertrophy and eccentric hypertrophy. In: Ostadal B, Dhalla NS, editors. Cardiac adaptations: molecular mechanisms. New York, NY: Springer New York; 2013. p. 147&#x2013;66.</Citation></Reference><Reference><Citation>Glickman MH, Ciechanover A. The ubiquitin-proteasome proteolytic pathway: destruction for the sake of construction. Physiol Rev. 2002;82:373&#x2013;428.</Citation><ArticleIdList><ArticleId IdType="doi">10.1152/physrev.00027.2001</ArticleId><ArticleId IdType="pubmed">11917093</ArticleId></ArticleIdList></Reference><Reference><Citation>Dorsch LM, Schuldt M, dos Remedios CG, Schinkel AFL, de Jong PL, Michels M, et al. Protein quality control activation and microtubule remodeling in hypertrophic cardiomyopathy. Cells. 2019;8:741.</Citation><ArticleIdList><ArticleId IdType="pmc">PMC6678711</ArticleId><ArticleId IdType="pubmed">31323898</ArticleId></ArticleIdList></Reference><Reference><Citation>Micheal S, Ayub H, Islam F, Siddiqui SN, Khan WA, Akhtar F, et al. Variants in the ASB10 Gene Are Associated with Primary Open Angle Glaucoma. PloS one. 2015;10:e0145005.</Citation><ArticleIdList><ArticleId IdType="doi">10.1371/journal.pone.0145005</ArticleId><ArticleId IdType="pmc">PMC4695091</ArticleId><ArticleId IdType="pubmed">26713451</ArticleId></ArticleIdList></Reference><Reference><Citation>Ferdous A, Wang Z, Luo Y, Li D, Luo X, Schiattarella G, et al. FoxO1-Dio2 signaling axis governs cardiomyocyte thyroid hormone