999-1.</Citation><ArticleIdList><ArticleId IdType="doi">10.1007/s12311-018-0999-1</ArticleId><ArticleId IdType="pubmed">30607797</ArticleId></ArticleIdList></Reference><Reference><Citation>Str&#xf6;mberg I, Almqvist P, Bygdeman M, Finger TE, Gerhardt G, Granholm AC, et al. Intracerebral xenografts of human mesencephalic tissue into athymic rats: immunochemical and in vivo electrochemical studies. Proc Natl Acad Sci USA. 1988;85:8331&#x2013;8334. doi: 10.1073/pnas.85.21.8331.</Citation><ArticleIdList><ArticleId IdType="doi">10.1073/pnas.85.21.8331</ArticleId><ArticleId IdType="pmc">PMC282423</ArticleId><ArticleId IdType="pubmed">3186728</ArticleId></ArticleIdList></Reference><Reference><Citation>Brundin P, Nilsson OG, Gage FH, Bj&#xf6;rklund A. Cyclosporin A increases survival of cross-species intrastriatal grafts of embryonic dopamine-containing neurons. Exp Brain Res. 1985;60:204&#x2013;208. doi: 10.1007/BF00237035.</Citation><ArticleIdList><ArticleId IdType="doi">10.1007/BF00237035</ArticleId><ArticleId IdType="pubmed">3930278</ArticleId></ArticleIdList></Reference><Reference><Citation>Itakura G, Kobayashi Y, Nishimura S, Iwai H, Takano M, Iwanami A, et al. Controlling immune rejection is a fail-safe system against potential tumorigenicity after human iPSC-derived neural stem cell transplantation. Muotri AR, editor. PLoS One. 2015;10:e0116413.</Citation><ArticleIdList><ArticleId IdType="pmc">PMC4338009</ArticleId><ArticleId IdType="pubmed">25706286</ArticleId></ArticleIdList></Reference><Reference><Citation>Heuer A, Kirkeby A, Pfisterer U, J&#xf6;nsson ME, Parmar M. hESC-derived neural progenitors prevent xenograft rejection through neonatal desensitisation. Exp Neurol. 2016;282:78&#x2013;85. doi: 10.1016/j.expneurol.2016.05.027.</Citation><ArticleIdList><ArticleId IdType="doi">10.1016/j.expneurol.2016.05.027</ArticleId><ArticleId IdType="pmc">PMC4920671</ArticleId><ArticleId IdType="pubmed">27235932</ArticleId></ArticleIdList></Reference><Reference><Citation>Sant